-- Desktop Auction / latest rationale with auction_capabilities role inheritance.
-- These eight authored requirements preserve the latest Desktop OCL bodies.
--
-- auctioneer and participant inherit the capability-role belief attributes.
-- Those attributes represent player beliefs, not authoritative Artifact state;
-- belief equality with the world is NOT assumed or imposed as an invariant.
-- Source literals, arguments and annotations are selected by declarative XML.
-- The Java engine must contain no Auction names or predicate-selection rules.
--
-- Operation self is the exact Auction Artifact projection, not a Role instance.
-- service/amount are actual invocation inputs; all three source operations return
-- void. Bind PRE/POST to the same invocation and its before/after cuts. No @pre
-- expression is required by these authored clauses; no return/caller is invented.
-- Operation success and Jason step success remain separate runtime evidence.
-- currentWinner is an internal field and winner is only published by stop.
-- A successful non-improving bid may leave every Artifact value unchanged.

context Auction::start(service : String)
pre Idle:
    not self.running
post Opened:
    self.running and self.task = service

context Auction::bid(amount : Real)
pre RunningForBid:
    self.running

context Auction::stop()
pre RunningForStop:
    self.running
post Closed:
    not self.running

-- Actual MOISE enabled/satisfied transition times, not operation return times
-- or TCP notification receipt times. -1 is known not-yet-occurred only under
-- complete history. Missing source evidence remains undefined/INCOMPLETE.
-- AuctionMonitor is an explicit observer view outside the CSL domain model.
context AuctionMonitor
inv SchemeOrder:
    (self.bidEnabledAt >= 0 implies
        self.startSatisfiedAt >= 0 and
        self.startSatisfiedAt <= self.bidEnabledAt) and
    (self.bidSatisfiedAt >= 0 implies
        self.bidEnabledAt >= 0 and
        self.bidEnabledAt <= self.bidSatisfiedAt) and
    (self.decideEnabledAt >= 0 implies
        self.bidSatisfiedAt >= 0 and
        self.bidSatisfiedAt <= self.decideEnabledAt) and
    (self.decideSatisfiedAt >= 0 implies
        self.decideEnabledAt >= 0 and
        self.decideEnabledAt <= self.decideSatisfiedAt)

-- Keep latest Desktop EXISTS semantics: at least one committed participant
-- has both observed MOISE done evidence and a successful real bid, unless the
-- exact successful administrative override is observed. The override permits
-- scheme progress; it does not satisfy D_bid or count as an actual bid.
-- Role population is not mission commitment. Freeze bidCommittedBy at the first
-- observed bid satisfaction; keep exact same-run/same-scheme player identities.
context AuctionMonitor
inv BidEvidence:
    self.bidDoneBy->forAll(a |
        self.actualBidBy->includes(a)) and
    (self.bidSatisfiedAt >= 0 implies
        self.adminBidOverride or
        self.bidCommittedBy->exists(a |
            self.bidDoneBy->includes(a) and
            self.actualBidBy->includes(a)))

-- AuctionObligation is a retained observer record, not a CSL Entity.
-- Only bid/decide obligations enter this view; XML selects them explicitly.
-- One record per actual activation, including later mission commitments.
-- Source NPL activation/deadline/first terminal use one qualified clock basis.
-- unfulfilled is latched; admin recovery does not erase an expired obligation.
-- Pending overtime also violates this requirement. Unknown is not Boolean false.
